cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "STANet: controlled evaluation of hybrid LSTM-GAT architectures for traffic anomaly detection"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package for a controlled, multi-seed evaluation of the design
  choices underlying a hybrid LSTM + Graph Attention Network traffic anomaly
  detector. Contains the full experiment pipeline (encoder benchmark, fusion
  ablation, graph-construction ablation, trip-grouped cross-validation over
  five seeds, repeated grouped partitions, graph ablations including edge
  removal and random topology, classical and rule-based references, inductive
  evaluation, equivalence testing, trip-level cluster statistics, efficiency
  measurements), the synthetic trajectory dataset generated over an
  OpenStreetMap-derived road network, three further generated datasets
  spanning a second road network, and every result file reported in the paper.
  Release v3.0.0 accompanies the revision: it adds the five-seed
  cross-validated analysis, the repeated-partition campaign with the
  Nadeau-Bengio correction for overlapping training sets, the replication
  study across four datasets, and the verification scripts that check every
  number in the manuscript and in the response letter against these files.
